##fileformat=VCFv4.2
##source=hand-picked, not synthetic coordinates: verified present in dbNSFP 5.3.1a on this
##  install (backend/bin/gen_dbnsfp_aligned_columns.py consumes the output of annotating these).
##  Each was chosen for a real multi-transcript row (Ensembl_transcriptid has >=2 entries) so the
##  script's DATA-derived check has more than one independent position to disqualify a coincidentally
##  matching column against - see the "Gene_other_names matches ~6% of rows" note in that script's
##  docstring for why a single variant is not enough. Six distinct genes, six chromosomes:
##    chr1:1623453 A>C   MIB2     (140 transcripts)
##    chr6:3006553 A>C   NQO2     (90 transcripts)
##    chr10:104032959 G>A COL17A1 (10 transcripts; the overlapping-gene case fixed by commit 5d823f7)
##    chr13:27665862 A>G POLR1D   (6 transcripts; overlaps a lncRNA - the SIDEVAR case this whole
##                                 mechanism exists for)
##    chr17:1744996 A>C  SERPINF2 (74 transcripts)
##    chr19:624800 C>A   POLRMT   (36 transcripts)
##  Regenerate this list only if dbNSFP drops one of these positions in a future release (unlikely -
##  they are all well-annotated, long-standing RefSeq/Ensembl genes, not release-fragile edge cases).
